rustc_llvm: a rustc hosted on EmiBSD links the system's shared libLLVM

Why a patch: the native toolchain's LLVM tools and rustc share one
libLLVM.so.<major>.<minor>, the system's library, which llvm/'s native
tree installs in /usr/lib (D-0012); librustc_driver no longer carries a
copy of LLVM. Whether rustc_llvm links LLVM shared or static is one switch
of bootstrap for every host it builds (llvm.link-shared, handed to this
build script as LLVM_LINK_SHARED), and the native rustc is cross-built on
a machine whose own stage 1 compiler links llvm/'s static libraries: there
is no shared LLVM for that machine, and no setting that says "shared for
this host only". The build script therefore links shared when the rustc
it builds is hosted on EmiBSD. Nothing changes for a rustc hosted
elsewhere, the cross toolchain's among them. EmiBSD-specific: not for
upstream. Written by EmiBSD (ISC) over upstream's text (Apache-2.0 OR
MIT), carried by DevTools over the pinned tag. Author: Emilio Navarrete
Lineros, 2026-11-15.

--- a/compiler/rustc_llvm/build.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_llvm/build.rs
@@ -36,7 +36,10 @@
 fn detect_llvm_link() -> (&'static str, &'static str) {
     // Force the link mode we want, preferring static by default, but
     // possibly overridden by `configure --enable-llvm-link-shared`.
-    if tracked_env_var_os("LLVM_LINK_SHARED").is_some() {
+    // A rustc hosted on EmiBSD links the system's shared libLLVM, whatever the machine that
+    // builds it links for its own compiler: bootstrap's switch is one for every host.
+    let emibsd_host = env::var("TARGET").is_ok_and(|target| target.contains("-emibsd-emibsd"));
+    if tracked_env_var_os("LLVM_LINK_SHARED").is_some() || emibsd_host {
         ("dylib", "--link-shared")
     } else {
         ("static", "--link-static")
